# xun, iPadOS 27.2.1 line (24B156) — the device layer of the XNU patch series.
#
# Same shape as UniXNU-muyu: this directory holds this board's patches, and the order is the
# filename order, so the list below is the directory listing and nothing else. A
# schema_version 2 board never globs a directory; board.toml names
# device:patches/xnu-27/series and the framework resolves it here.
# scripts/check-board-os.py fails if this file and `ls *.patch` ever disagree.
#
# The arch, soc and os layers are NOT copied in. board.toml references them by prefix and the
# framework resolves each into its own checkout, exactly as UniXNU-uke does.
#
# Five patches, and what each one is for on THIS board:
#
#   xun-console-clear        No UART in the XNU closure for SM6225, so the panel is the only
#                            output there is. DarwinBoot leaves its handoff text on it in a
#                            larger font and the kernel console draws over it.
#   xun-source-storage-start NativeEmmc and RamBlock are built in, and their class registration
#                            lives in native_source_storage_start(). Without it IOKit matches the
#                            personality but not the class, and nothing publishes the volumes.
#   native-stack-shift       A 4 KiB kernel on 32 KiB-aligned stacks. AMFI's PAGE_SHIFT_CONST
#                            reader bounds-checks against the stack and fails at fixed call
#                            depths without this. NOTE: the patch only *defines* the symbol. The
#                            binding that makes it take effect is a prelink fixture entry for the
#                            one GOT slot AMFI reads PAGE_SHIFT_CONST from, and that fixture is
#                            generated from a built kernelcache - so it is a build-time step after
#                            the first kernel build, alongside [kernel.prelink] kernelcache_sha256.
#                            Defining the symbol without the binding changes nothing; it is here
#                            because the binding resolves it by name.
#   offline-no-iortc-wait    There is no IORTC device on SM6225 and the wait never matches.
#                            Measured on muyu as a data abort inside IOKitInitializeTime; the
#                            reasoning is the same here - a wait for a service that cannot exist
#                            is not a boot step.
#   darwin27-missing-syscalls
#                            The 24B156 userland calls syscall numbers 556 and 557, which
#                            xnu-12377 does not declare; `nosys` would kill the caller with
#                            SIGSYS. Found with tools/ipados27/abi-census.py over the shipped
#                            dyld shared cache. The patch body explains how.

xun-console-clear.patch
xun-source-storage-start.patch
native-stack-shift.patch
offline-no-iortc-wait.patch
darwin27-missing-syscalls.patch
